{{!
    @template mod_examcheck/seat_assign

    Seat assignment page: the assignment count above the seat dynamic table. Each row of
    the table server-renders a select holding only the currently assigned student; the JS
    enhances it into an AJAX autocomplete, saves changes instantly, and re-enhances every
    row after the table body reloads on sort or paging.

    Never let two closing braces meet inside a comment such as this one. Mustache closes a
    comment at the first pair it meets, and the rest of the block would then be rendered
    as literal text. Keep the example context flat, with no nested objects.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-region="examcheck-seat-assign" - the page root, carries data-cmid

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cmid - course module id
    * assignedcount - number of assigned seats
    * seatcount - total number of seats
    * table - the rendered seat_assign dynamic table

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cmid": 12,
        "assignedcount": 1,
        "seatcount": 2,
        "table": "<table class=\"generaltable\"><tbody><tr><td>A1</td></tr></tbody></table>"
    }
}}
<div data-region="examcheck-seat-assign" data-cmid="{{cmid}}">
    <p class="text-muted">
        {{#str}} seatassignedcount, mod_examcheck, { "assigned": {{assignedcount}}, "total": {{seatcount}} } {{/str}}
    </p>
    {{{table}}}
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['mod_examcheck/seat_assign'], function(SeatAssign) {
    SeatAssign.init({{cmid}});
});
{{/js}}
